        "section": "rule",
        "sentence_id": "p8_r2"
      },
      "text": "Three important dlls file to diffing/compare with MFC malware, for example in this sample eToken , are mfc42.dll , mfc42d.dll , mfco42d.dll . You can find and download the correct debug symbol file ( .pdb ) of the dlls you have. The most important one is mfc42d.dll ( debug build ), since its .pdb will contain full information about the types, enumes, classes, and vtables of the MFC classes. We export local types from mfc42d.dll to .h file, then import into our idb database. IDA's Parse C ++ has an error, unable to parse the \" <> \" template syntax, so we find and replace pairs of \" < \" and \" > \" to \" _ \" in .h files.",
